      "evidence": "Transcribed from 'Annex A - MAP OF DESIGNATED AREAS AND LISTS OF ROADS WITHIN THE DESIGNATED AREAS' of Leicester City Council's statutory designation notice, linked as 'Read the designation notice' from https://www.leicester.gov.uk/your-community/housing/landlords/selective-licensing/. The notice records the designation as made 7 July 2022, in force 10 October 2022 and ceasing 9 October 2027, covering parts of Stoneygate (East Cluster); Westcotes, Fosse, Braunstone Park & Rowley Fields (West Cluster); and Saffron (South Cluster). Annex A's 'List of Road in the Designated Selective Licensing Areas' runs over three pages as ruled tables with 'Street Name' and 'Included Part Street' columns; pairings were read from the PDF's actual cell borders rather than from flowed text, because plain-text extraction misaligns the wrapped number ranges and mis-assigns them to neighbouring streets (for example it wrongly attaches '3 -37 odd' to Hopefield Road instead of Imperial Avenue). 197 table rows yielded 192 distinct streets; the council's own list repeats Narborough Road, New Park Road, Newport Street, Noble Street and St James Road, and those duplicates are collapsed. 23 distinct streets carry a part-street restriction (24 table rows, one being the repeated Narborough Road entry), reproduced verbatim including the council's irregular spacing and the stray hyphen in Denton Street's '1 -3 odd and 2 - 4 - even'. Streets with a blank 'Included Part Street' cell are designated in full and have numbers null. This is the Part 3 licensing designation, not Leicester's separate Article 4 HMO planning direction."
